 # On-call alerting
 
 Alerts go to the paging gateway.
-If the gateway is down or draining, the sender retries with doubling waits and drops the alert about seven seconds after it was raised.
+If the gateway is down or draining, the sender retries with doubling waits and drops the alert about thirty-one seconds after it was raised.
 Each drop is logged as `alert_dropped`; check the log before assuming an alert was never raised.
 
 ## Capacity
 
